  "heading_latex": "\\textrm{Axiom Schema of Separation}",
  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "Axiom:\ngiven:\n. A is \\set\n. phi(x_) is (_ is \\set) -> (_ is \\\\statement)\nthen:\n. exists: B is \\set\n  suchThat:\n  . forAll: x is \\set\n    then:\n    . have: x \"in\" B\n      iff:\n      . x \"in\"? A\n      . phi(x)\nDocumented:\n. called: \"Axiom Schema of Separation\"\n. description: \"For every property $\\varphi$, the elements of an existing set\n                $A$ satisfying $\\varphi$ form a set.\"\nId: \"5077fbc7-a5c8-4d60-b1a7-a9d65097f003\"",
